### Check 4 — Security high findings

{% if light_check | default(false) %}Read only this scan's rows: the last N lines of `{{ WTR }}/.claude/observability/security/findings-<today>.jsonl`
(`<today>` is the UTC date, `date -u +%F`), where N is the count on the scan's `Security scan: N finding(s)`
line. The file's earlier lines are earlier scans', from this checkout or a stale one. N = 0 → PASS.{% else %}Read the most recent `.claude/observability/security/findings-*.jsonl`.{% endif %}

FAIL when: any finding has `severity == "high"` AND `resolution != "accepted-risk-with-rationale"`. Resolutions must be deliberate (recorded in PLAN ADR or wrapup commit body).

PASS when: zero unresolved high findings.
